# topogend session token (autogenerated, owner-readable)
/.topogend-token

# Pulse-probe dump from the visual editor's webview (workspace-local, transient)
# Anchored on purpose: the repo root is the ONLY place a probe dir belongs (see
# tools/topology-vscode/src/repo-root.ts). One written anywhere else is a bug,
# and leaving it unignored is what surfaces it — it shows up as an untracked
# dir and blocks tools/new-task.sh instead of sitting there unnoticed.
/.probe/

# Prebuilt Go binary cache (built once by the editor runner; not for VCS)
/.wirefold-cache/

# Scene sidecar — gitignored so camera/label state does not generate commit noise.
# Diagram state (positions, fades) stays in topology.json.
/topology.scene.json

# Tree-topology scene sidecar (auto-written by Go on each run; not for VCS).
/topology/view/scene.json
/topology/view/scene.json.tmp

# One-file-per-writer split of the scene sidecar above: each of these has exactly ONE
# writer, which is what let sceneFileMu be deleted rather than narrowed. camera/overlays/
# sphere are the same kind of auto-written, locally-preferred view state scene.json was —
# not for VCS.
# nodes/<id>/position.json and local-polars.json are NOT listed here: they carry the same
# authoritative per-node data meta.json does (which IS tracked), so they stay trackable too.
/topology/view/camera.json
/topology/view/camera.json.tmp
/topology/view/overlays.json
/topology/view/overlays.json.tmp
/topology/view/sphere.json
/topology/view/sphere.json.tmp

# Hook block log (local audit trail, not for VCS)
.claude/hooks/go-blocks.log

# Editor settings
.vscode/

# macOS
.DS_Store

.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Agent worktrees (temporary, per-agent scratch checkouts)
.claude/worktrees/

# Python bytecode from the delegation hooks (scripts/*.py).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# LIVE SCENE STATE, written continuously by the running sim — untracked on purpose.
#
# view/*.json (camera pose, overlay flags, scene sphere, selected tab) is written by the
# view-owner goroutine and is rewritten while you orbit or toggle anything, so it stays
# .gitignore'd the ordinary way.
#
# A node's own position and each of its outgoing edges' geometry deltas used to live in a
# SEPARATE gitignored overlay file (position.json / <label>.geom.json) next to the tracked
# seed (meta.json / <label>.json). That split is gone: position and delta now live directly
# in meta.json and <label>.json — the same file that holds type/id/gate/orbit or
# target/sourceHandle/kind — so a fresh clone still loads a laid-out scene from one file per
# owner, not two. Untracking a runtime write to that ONE file can no longer be done by path
# (the tracked seed and the drag output are the same path now); instead Go marks the file
# git-skip-worktree (`nodes/Wiring/gitskip`) right after writing it, so git stops reporting
# it modified. That is why these paths are NOT listed in this file — .gitignore can't express
# "ignore future writes to a path that starts out tracked", only skip-worktree can.
topology*/view/*.json

# Whether a node's orbit rule is currently ACTIVE is persisted output, deliberately separate
# from the rule's VALUES (orbit.phi/orbit.maxTheta), which stay in the tracked meta.json seed.
topology*/nodes/*/rule-active.json

# Where the running extension listens for "open this file as a tab", and that
# session's token. Written on activation, removed on shutdown.
docs/pair-node/port.js
